+---
+id: dl-001-run-typescript-sources-directly-via-node-s-native-type-stripping-no-build-step
+type: decision-log
+title: "Run TypeScript sources directly via Node's native type-stripping, no build step"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Context
+
+`package.json` declares `"test": "node --test"` and the repo ships no `typescript` devDependency,
+no build script, and no `dist/` output checked in. `tsconfig.json` already targets `NodeNext`
+modules with `declaration`/`outDir` set, which is the shape used once this package is built for
+consumers, but nothing currently invokes `tsc`. Node 22.23 (the version available here) runs `.ts`
+files directly, stripping types natively, including under `node --test` when the test files
+themselves use the `.test.ts` suffix.
+
+## Decision
+
+For this feature (`resolvePointer`) the test file imports the implementation with an explicit
+`./index.ts` extension and both files run unmodified under `node --test` via Node's native
+TypeScript support — no compile step, no new devDependency, no change to `tsconfig.json` or
+`package.json`. I verified `src/index.ts` type-checks cleanly against the project's existing strict
+`tsconfig.json` using a temporary, uncommitted `typescript` install; I did not add `typescript`,
+`@types/node`, or a typecheck script to the project, since none of the existing scripts call for
+one and introducing build tooling was out of scope for this task.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- `npm test` keeps working with zero dependencies, matching the project's "no runtime dependency"
+  description.
+- Relative imports in source/test files must keep using the real `.ts` extension (not `.js`) for
+  Node's native loader to resolve them; this will not type-check under a future `tsc --build` step
+  unless that step later enables `allowImportingTsExtensions` (or the project switches to emitting
+  `.js` and importing that instead). Whoever wires up a real build/typecheck script should revisit
+  this.
+- Follow-on features that build on `resolvePointer` should keep following the same `*.test.ts`
+  pattern importing with `.ts` extensions, for consistency, until a build step changes the
+  convention.
